  "prefLabel": "Hedc 305.01 Who May File a Complaint",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Hedc 305.01 Who May File a Complaint.\n\n(a) Any person who has a complaint against a school who has first sought redress directly from said school through its complaint process, and said process has been completed and was found to be in favor of the school, may file a complaint with the office.\n\nSource. #10520, eff 2-12-14 (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Hedc 300); ss by #12644, eff 10-11-18 (formerly Hedc 308.01)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/hedc300.html"
